        "testata": "France 24",
        "lingua_originale": "en",
        "titolo_orig": "‘Disturbing trend’ of US-Israeli strikes hitting non-military targets in Iran",
        "testo_it": "Preoccupanti attacchi USA-Israele su obiettivi non militari in Iran.",
        "priorita": "Alta",
        "id_gruppo": 9,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/disturbing-trend-of-us-israeli-strikes-hitting-non-military-targets-in-iran",
        "orario": "07:38",
        "timestamp": 1775194726,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. ‘Disturbing trend’ of US-Israeli strikes hitting non-military targets in Iran Middle East Issued on: 03/04/2026 - 07:38 Modified: 03/04/2026 - 07:45 Reporting from Tehran early Friday, FRANCE 24’s Reza Sayah says there’s been a “disturbing trend” in recent days of US-Israeli strikes hitting non-military targets across Iran. A strike on Iran’s tallest bridge last night killed eight people and wounded 90 others, said Sayah. The war has seen US-Israeli strikes target Iran's civilian airports, fuel depots, hospitals, sports facilities, pharmaceutical manufacturing companies, universities and schools, he notes. Europe, NATO under pressure over Iran war: 'Trump strong with the weak and weak with the strong' 02/04/2026 Middle East Israel's Lebanon endgame: 'Dismantle Hezbollah entirely as a political and social movement' 02/04/2026 Middle East US and Israel 'again bombing what were clearly non-military sites' in Iran 02/04/2026 Middle East US war on Iran: 'Absolute disaster' for Middle Eastern airlines 02/04/2026 Middle East Trump claims Iran wants a ceasefire, Iran says remarks are ‘false and baseless’ 01/04/2026 Middle East 'Strategy of ecological terror. Desalination as a weapon of war' in the Middle East 01/04/2026 Middle East US journalist Shelly Kittleson kidnapped in Iraq 01/04/2026 Middle East Death penalty 'a deep stain on the law books of the state of Israel' 01/04/2026 Middle East ‘Blatantly racist’: Death penalty law among 'worst legislation' in Israeli parliamentary history 01/04/2026 Middle East"
